\fs36 \cf0 1.1 Inputs\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Input\
Mapping\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Left pad
\f1\b0  (labels FWD / turn / BACK)\
up/down = forward/back (vx) \'b7 left/right = turn (wz)\

\f0\b Right pad
\f1\b0  (labels FWD / slide / BACK)\
left/right = slide sideways (vy) \'b7 up/down = forward/back \'97 the stronger of the two pads wins for vx\

\f0\b \uc0\u8612  Slide left / \u8614  Slide right
\f1\b0  buttons\
hold to side-walk at 0.4 m/s \'d7 speed-scale (sends lateral velocity; in Retroid mode the side axis of the 42-byte frame)\

\f0\b Keyboard
\f1\b0 \
W/S or \uc0\u8593 /\u8595  = forward/back \'b7 A/D or \u8592 /\u8594  = turn \'b7 Space (hold) = E-STOP\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Pads and keys can be mixed; diagonals combine axes (e.g. forward + slide).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1.2 Per-axis processing (identical for both pads)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	1	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Vector from pointer:
\f1\b0  each pad returns x/y in \uc0\u8722 1\'85+1 relative to its centre.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	2	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Deadzone:
\f1\b0  magnitude below 
\f0\b 0.08
\f1\b0  = neutral (no command).\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	3	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Normalisation:
\f1\b0  the magnitude past the deadzone is rescaled so small pushes still count: s = (m \uc0\u8722  0.08) / (1 \u8722  0.08), clamped to 1.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	4	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Stick curve:
\f1\b0  s = s ^ curve when curve > 1 (default 
\f0\b 1.25
\f1\b0 , \'93Soft\'94) \'97 finer control near the centre.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	5	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Speed scale:
\f1\b0  multiply by the scale setting (50 / 75 / 
\f0\b 100
\f1\b0  / 150 %).\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	6	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Axis assignment:
\f1\b0  vx = \uc0\u8722 y \'d7 s \'d7 scale \'b7 wz = x \'d7 s \'d7 scale (left pad) \'b7 vy = x \'d7 s \'d7 scale (right pad).\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	7	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Reverse-steer mirror:
\f1\b0  when reversing (vx < 0) the steering sign is flipped, so \'93left\'94 still turns the robot left while backing up.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	8	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Clamps (server side):
\f1\b0  vx \uc0\u8804  
\f0\b 0.5 m/s
\f1\b0  \'b7 vy \uc0\u8804  
\f0\b 0.4 m/s
\f1\b0  \'b7 wz \uc0\u8804  
\f0\b 0.8 rad/s
\f1\b0  \'b7 per-axis 
\f0\b sign
\f1\b0  (Forward / Turn / Lateral) applied on send.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1.3 Sending\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Commands are produced by a 
\f0\b 60 ms
\f1\b0  loop; additionally a drive update fires immediately on press and on every move event (zero-latency response).\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The engine streams at up to 
\f0\b 50 Hz
\f1\b0  (rate_hz) while the request is fresh, keeping the robot in auto mode (0x21010C03 interleaved) with a heartbeat (0x21040001) every 
\f0\b 300 ms
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Tail:
\f1\b0  the last velocity is kept alive for 
\f0\b 300 ms
\f1\b0  after the last input, then zeroed; when a velocity stream ends the engine also fires the 
\f0\b official brake frames
\f1\b0  (0x21010C0B, values 0 and 1) for ~0.35 s so the robot cannot coast.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1.4 Release & stopping\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Pads are 
\f0\b spring-centred
\f1\b0 : on release the knob animates home (160 ms) and the robot stops \'97 a stop command is sent immediately, not on the next tick.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Release anywhere (window-level capture), losing window focus, hiding the tab, 
\f0\b STOP
\f1\b0 , or 
\f0\b E-STOP
\f1\b0  all stop the robot.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
E-STOP
\f1\b0  latches: every command is refused and stop frames keep being sent until 
\f0\b \uc0\u10226  Return
\f1\b0 ; a latched E-stop also cancels a running action.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1.5 Drive modes (Advanced \uc0\u8594  Joystick mode)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Velocity frames (proven)
\f1\b0  \'97 sends 0x140 (x), 0x145 (y), 0x141 (yaw), each type 1 with one 
\f0\b f64
\f1\b0  payload (value field 8), plus the auto-mode frame.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Retroid / official SDK
\f1\b0  \'97 sends the same 42-byte frames as the physical remote to UDP 
\f0\b 12121
\f1\b0 : header 0x55 0x66, ctrl, data_len 32, seq, id 1, checksum (byte-sum of payload); payload = 10 \'d7 u16 buttons + 4 \'d7 i16 axes (left_x, left_y, right_x, right_y) + 2 \'d7 u16 axis buttons; range \'b11000. Mapping: left_y = forward, right_x = yaw (sign configurable), left_x = slide. The robot's own controller then interprets the sticks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1.6 Velocity semantics\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Velocity commands are honoured 
\f0\b only while the robot is standing
\f1\b0  (in auto mode); while sitting/lying they are ignored silently.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
UDP gives 
\f0\b no acknowledgement
\f1\b0 ; confirm motion visually or via telemetry.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

