\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2.6 Execution rules that apply to every command\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Posture handling:
\f1\b0  an action declares its required pose; the console re-poses only when the tracked state is known to differ, or always when force_posture is set (rolls, jumps, hello). With an unknown state and no force, the action is sent directly (press STAND/SIT first if the robot is in the other pose).\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Replay:
\f1\b0  poses/rolls are re-sent 3\'d7 at ~1 Hz (\'93slow replay\'94); modes/gaits are single-shot; other frames use a short burst.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Cancellation:
\f1\b0  E-STOP aborts any action mid-play.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Safety:
\f1\b0  keep the area clear and the physical E-stop within reach for any moving command.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

